WEBVTT

00:00:03.340 --> 00:00:06.260
STUDIO RIKKA

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:12.440
In the future, probably Japan.

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:15.000
Robots have long been put into practical use,

00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:19.600
and practical use of androids has just begun.

00:00:56.970 --> 00:00:58.970
Master, the log has been correctly outputted.

00:00:59.560 --> 00:01:00.560
Question.

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:03.010
What is it?

00:01:10.300 --> 00:01:11.700
Cancel the question.

00:01:11.840 --> 00:01:12.840
Coffee.

00:01:12.940 --> 00:01:14.520
Understood.

00:01:22.420 --> 00:01:23.220
Where's everyone?

00:01:23.420 --> 00:01:24.220
No, I mean . . .

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:26.210
Status, family.

00:01:26.420 --> 00:01:29.110
Father stayed overnight at work.

00:01:29.240 --> 00:01:33.000
Mother went out before my activation.

00:01:33.340 --> 00:01:35.910
It seems Miss Naoko is still in bed.

00:01:36.530 --> 00:01:37.560
Her time of return?

00:01:37.750 --> 00:01:39.250
3:18 AM

00:01:39.700 --> 00:01:41.200
Ugh, I feel so sick.

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:42.550
Then don't go out drinking.

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:45.390
But I feel so good at first.

00:01:48.210 --> 00:01:49.980
Hey, ask for your own coffee!

00:01:50.370 --> 00:01:51.570
This thing,

00:01:51.770 --> 00:01:53.770
it came to get me after the party.

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:56.430
I was so embarrassed!

00:01:57.180 --> 00:01:58.680
What would you like for breakfast?

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:00.500
Cancel breakfast.

00:02:00.690 --> 00:02:01.690
Excuse me. Please say that again -

00:02:02.070 --> 00:02:03.570
Breakfast for one, right away.

00:02:03.750 --> 00:02:05.260
Understood.

00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:10.500
Domestically produced food has topped 80%,

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:13.500
according to the Food Management Bureau.

00:02:15.260 --> 00:02:18.600
Would you eat a tomato created by a machine?

00:02:21.290 --> 00:02:23.670
Warmth, especially for our era.

00:02:24.460 --> 00:02:25.480
Ethics Committee

00:02:26.360 --> 00:02:29.360
So "dori-kei" comes from "android-holic,"

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.500
or dependence on androids, right. Right?

00:02:32.700 --> 00:02:35.000
This is what we call young people

00:02:35.170 --> 00:02:37.470
who treat house-roids like humans.

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:40.500
We did a story on "android-holic" people.

00:02:41.500 --> 00:02:45.500
Yuck! It's like, get away from me!

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:47.970
They're arm in arm, and stuff like that.

00:02:48.800 --> 00:02:50.000
No way!

00:02:50.500 --> 00:02:52.500
They're probably lonely, without any friends.

00:02:53.540 --> 00:02:54.840
You should be careful too.

00:02:55.030 --> 00:02:56.980
Hey, what are you getting at?

00:03:44.870 --> 00:03:46.870
Rikuo, I saw your sister yesterday.

00:03:47.500 --> 00:03:49.000
Late at night, right?

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:50.400
At the train station. She was pretty drunk.

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:52.000
She had an escort home!

00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:52.700
Who, you?

00:03:52.800 --> 00:03:53.800
Our android.

00:03:54.220 --> 00:03:55.900
That's what I'm saying.

00:03:57.570 --> 00:03:59.270
You trust robots too much.

00:03:59.540 --> 00:04:01.540
It's not like I trust them.

00:04:01.960 --> 00:04:02.960
Look, what's it called, that law -

00:04:03.180 --> 00:04:04.630
The Three Laws of Robots

00:04:04.710 --> 00:04:05.710
The First Law.

00:04:05.800 --> 00:04:08.360
Don't allow humans to be harmed. Protect humans.

00:04:08.750 --> 00:04:09.900
I get it . . . so that's why it escorted her home.

00:04:10.100 --> 00:04:12.100
But it's not like they worry about humans.

00:04:12.300 --> 00:04:13.590
Think about it - after all, you've got a robot.

00:04:13.790 --> 00:04:16.050
You're a fine one to talk! You don't even have one.

00:04:18.610 --> 00:04:19.840
Hey, what do you think about this?

00:04:20.080 --> 00:04:21.080
It's a bunch of numbers.

00:04:21.290 --> 00:04:22.790
It's the log of our android's movements.

00:04:23.130 --> 00:04:24.750
What part?

00:04:28.410 --> 00:04:29.810
Hey, are you busy?

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:31.500
I want you to come along with me.

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:33.200
Where to?

00:04:33.600 --> 00:04:34.900
I'm not sure . . .

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:36.000
What's up with that?

00:04:36.200 --> 00:04:38.600
It's been acting weird, coming home at odd hours.

00:04:38.800 --> 00:04:39.800
Your robot?

00:04:40.010 --> 00:04:42.610
So I got curious and looked up its movement log.

00:04:43.300 --> 00:04:44.410
And then -

00:04:44.520 --> 00:04:48.580
About 20 hours ago, that'd be yesterday afternoon . . .

00:04:48.670 --> 00:04:50.030
It made a detour, on its own.

00:04:50.230 --> 00:04:52.830
So . . . it must have had something to do.

00:04:59.570 --> 00:05:00.430
Here?

00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:10.200
Seriously, here?

00:05:10.400 --> 00:05:11.900
Maybe the GPS is off?

00:05:12.100 --> 00:05:14.100
This is no place for a robot to come.

00:05:41.500 --> 00:05:43.300
Time of Eve

00:05:43.550 --> 00:05:45.050
Seems strange, huh?

00:05:45.200 --> 00:05:47.190
Gotta go in to know for sure.

00:05:51.800 --> 00:05:52.800
Maybe it is strange.

00:05:53.000 --> 00:05:54.000
So should we leave?

00:05:54.200 --> 00:05:57.000
No discrimination between humans and robots.

00:05:57.300 --> 00:05:59.700
Obey the rule and enjoy yourself!

00:06:06.780 --> 00:06:10.020
Time of Eve

00:06:18.500 --> 00:06:19.500
Is this a . . . ?

00:06:19.800 --> 00:06:20.800
Welcome!

00:06:21.600 --> 00:06:23.000
Feel free to take any of the empty seats.

00:06:23.200 --> 00:06:25.200
I'll go take your order.

00:06:27.120 --> 00:06:28.530
Right over there.

00:06:28.610 --> 00:06:31.420
You might not be here for long,

00:06:31.870 --> 00:06:33.790
but enjoy yourselves.

00:06:46.400 --> 00:06:47.100
A cafe?

00:06:47.300 --> 00:06:48.300
A cafe.

00:06:48.500 --> 00:06:49.500
An android coming to a cafe?

00:06:49.700 --> 00:06:51.200
Probably not to have tea.

00:06:51.500 --> 00:06:52.900
And then there's that rule.

00:06:53.100 --> 00:06:54.100
So you think it's bad news after all?

00:06:54.300 --> 00:06:57.900
In terms of robotic law, it's the grey zone.

00:06:58.000 --> 00:06:59.200
The cafe's rule is too vague.

00:06:59.400 --> 00:06:59.800
Hey, listen to me!

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:00.800
It's here.

00:07:01.600 --> 00:07:04.000
Over there . . . it's the android we just saw.

00:07:11.000 --> 00:07:12.220
There's no ring.

00:07:12.600 --> 00:07:13.720
No kidding.

00:07:14.930 --> 00:07:16.260
Is this the grey zone?

00:07:16.410 --> 00:07:19.030
Have you ever seen a robot without a ring?

00:07:20.060 --> 00:07:21.890
That's a major violation of robotic law.

00:07:22.120 --> 00:07:24.130
Can't tell the difference between robots and humans.

00:07:25.080 --> 00:07:26.930
What's that robot doing?

00:07:28.150 --> 00:07:30.150
Are you ready to order?

00:07:32.000 --> 00:07:33.500
This Eve . . . Blend?

00:07:33.700 --> 00:07:35.050
Eve's Blend.

00:07:35.900 --> 00:07:36.600
That one.

00:07:36.800 --> 00:07:37.500
Same here.

00:07:37.700 --> 00:07:39.080
Two Evele!

00:07:40.810 --> 00:07:42.390
Don't break the rule, OK?

00:07:46.700 --> 00:07:47.700
Something bad just occurred to me.

00:07:47.900 --> 00:07:48.400
What?

00:07:49.300 --> 00:07:50.300
This cafe's rule.

00:07:50.500 --> 00:07:52.300
Don't discriminate between humans and robots?

00:07:53.200 --> 00:07:55.000
That's why there's no ring.

00:07:55.200 --> 00:07:56.200
You mean . . .?

00:07:56.500 --> 00:07:58.300
But even if that's the case . . .

00:07:58.300 --> 00:07:58.800
Aki, wake up!

00:07:59.000 --> 00:08:00.800
maybe it's not just a problem with that one.

00:08:01.000 --> 00:08:01.800
Meaning what?

00:08:02.000 --> 00:08:05.640
If all the other customers are following the rule . . . then what?

00:08:11.800 --> 00:08:12.800
Those kids over there . . .

00:08:13.000 --> 00:08:13.700
They're looking at us.

00:08:20.000 --> 00:08:21.000
Is this cafe bad news?

00:08:21.200 --> 00:08:22.000
Could be.

00:08:22.200 --> 00:08:23.800
About all this stuff . . .

00:08:24.000 --> 00:08:24.600
What?

00:08:25.200 --> 00:08:26.600
Should we say anything to your dad?

00:08:26.900 --> 00:08:27.900
This is has nothing to do with him!

00:08:28.100 --> 00:08:28.600
What?

00:08:29.000 --> 00:08:30.500
Are you newcomers? Nagi told me about you guys.

00:08:30.700 --> 00:08:32.600
Nagi's the girl at the counter.

00:08:32.800 --> 00:08:34.800
Can I sit here?

00:08:37.500 --> 00:08:39.000
How'd you find this place? You're somebody's friend?

00:08:39.200 --> 00:08:40.100
No, we just got here, and -

00:08:40.300 --> 00:08:42.700
Really? There haven't been any new people for ages!

00:08:42.800 --> 00:08:43.300
Is that so -

00:08:43.800 --> 00:08:45.300
It's always the same people.

00:08:45.500 --> 00:08:48.200
Setoro, reading a book. Shimei on the 2nd floor -

00:08:48.400 --> 00:08:50.300
and cutie pie Chie!

00:08:50.500 --> 00:08:52.500
And that's Koji and Rina over there. They're so close!

00:08:52.700 --> 00:08:53.700
There's Nagi, and who else?

00:08:53.900 --> 00:08:54.900
The girl in the hat.

00:08:55.100 --> 00:08:57.260
I'm Akiko! Nice to meet you!

00:08:59.500 --> 00:09:00.200
I'm Rikuo.

00:09:00.300 --> 00:09:00.920
Masaki.

00:09:01.180 --> 00:09:03.550
Rikuo and Masaki. Got it!

00:09:03.620 --> 00:09:04.820
Say . . .

00:09:05.760 --> 00:09:06.990
Have you seen a female android here?

00:09:07.200 --> 00:09:08.750
One point deducted.

00:09:10.330 --> 00:09:11.680
You broke the rule.

00:09:11.900 --> 00:09:12.400
Apologies.

00:09:12.600 --> 00:09:16.250
No need to put it like that - they're still newbies.

00:09:16.500 --> 00:09:18.100
But . . .

00:09:18.570 --> 00:09:21.120
Rule violations cause trouble for everyone!

00:09:21.500 --> 00:09:23.620
Nagi . . .

00:09:24.790 --> 00:09:27.960
She's good at heart. She cares a lot for the cafe.

00:09:28.070 --> 00:09:30.670
That considered, she doesn't do much work.

00:09:33.830 --> 00:09:36.080
She's sulking again.

00:09:36.720 --> 00:09:38.480
Nagi!

00:09:40.300 --> 00:09:41.800
I guess this place doesn't seem so bad.

00:09:42.000 --> 00:09:44.500
To the contrary, here's what I have to say.

00:09:44.700 --> 00:09:46.400
Why'd she come to a place like this?

00:09:46.600 --> 00:09:47.200
What are you getting at?

00:09:47.400 --> 00:09:49.220
I've got it.

00:09:49.630 --> 00:09:52.870
She's friendly with robots - an android-holic.

00:09:53.000 --> 00:09:53.700
You taking her side?

00:09:53.900 --> 00:09:55.300
No - that's not it!

00:09:55.800 --> 00:09:57.200
Well, ask her and you'll see.

00:09:57.800 --> 00:09:59.300
I'll get the same response - that it's a rule violation.

00:09:59.500 --> 00:10:01.500
There are other ways of asking.

00:10:01.870 --> 00:10:03.210
She's here.

00:10:03.580 --> 00:10:05.580
I got our drinks!

00:10:05.800 --> 00:10:07.470
She says she's sorry.

00:10:12.840 --> 00:10:15.280
I - um - it was my fault too!

00:10:16.020 --> 00:10:17.620
What are you getting all bashful about?

00:10:18.000 --> 00:10:18.900
Say, that hat suits you.

00:10:19.150 --> 00:10:21.150
Doesn't it? I agree!

00:10:21.410 --> 00:10:22.010
So . . .

00:10:23.200 --> 00:10:24.000
What?

00:10:24.200 --> 00:10:26.600
Well, talking about things beyond the cafe,

00:10:26.800 --> 00:10:28.500
I don't have an android at home.

00:10:28.700 --> 00:10:30.650
It's unusual these days.

00:10:33.410 --> 00:10:35.810
Akiko, you must have one at home.

00:10:39.710 --> 00:10:41.940
We sure do. That's why I'm here.

00:10:44.330 --> 00:10:45.430
What do you mean?

00:10:45.590 --> 00:10:48.420
Here, you can talk with everyone, right?

00:10:48.600 --> 00:10:50.100
So you learn lots of different things, right?

00:10:50.500 --> 00:10:51.300
Like what?

00:10:51.500 --> 00:10:54.900
Like . . . other people's feelings, I guess.

00:10:55.300 --> 00:10:57.540
Just talking about my home,

00:10:57.740 --> 00:11:01.240
for me, humans and androids are all family.

00:11:01.500 --> 00:11:04.300
But no matter how much they look like me,

00:11:04.500 --> 00:11:06.490
inside we're completely different.

00:11:06.890 --> 00:11:09.890
We look alike, but inside we're different.

00:11:09.930 --> 00:11:12.290
So a lot of times this is what goes through my mind.

00:11:12.580 --> 00:11:15.190
"What do you think about me?"

00:11:17.350 --> 00:11:19.700
So that's why I'm here.

00:11:20.280 --> 00:11:23.180
I want to talk with them, and understand them.

00:11:23.410 --> 00:11:26.500
After all, we're family.

00:11:31.890 --> 00:11:34.160
Ah, it's starting to rain.

00:11:36.240 --> 00:11:38.200
Hey, your robot isn't coming?

00:11:39.110 --> 00:11:41.480
She wants to know what they're thinking about.

00:11:41.510 --> 00:11:42.260
What do you think?

00:11:42.820 --> 00:11:44.250
About Akiko.

00:11:44.570 --> 00:11:46.070
Oh, you're talking about yesterday.

00:11:46.190 --> 00:11:47.990
You think someone like her is an android-holic?

00:11:48.300 --> 00:11:50.860
I don't have a robot, so it's hard for me to say.

00:11:51.620 --> 00:11:52.320
Master, I brought your umbrella.

00:11:52.500 --> 00:11:54.970
Better than treating them like that.

00:11:58.070 --> 00:12:00.990
Maybe she's a . . . considerate person?

00:12:01.120 --> 00:12:02.720
Sure, she's a nice person.

00:12:02.760 --> 00:12:03.560
That's it!

00:12:03.760 --> 00:12:05.620
Why are you so relieved?

00:12:05.820 --> 00:12:06.620
That's not what I mean!

00:12:06.860 --> 00:12:08.560
You're right, she was cute.

00:12:08.720 --> 00:12:09.320
Going to see her again today?

00:12:09.580 --> 00:12:11.240
Hey! That's not what I meant!

00:12:19.400 --> 00:12:20.060
Aki...

00:12:30.650 --> 00:12:33.480
I apologize for making you wait, Mast -

00:12:33.810 --> 00:12:35.810
Bag. Waterproof it. Return home by yourself.

00:12:36.070 --> 00:12:37.950
Understood.

00:12:55.970 --> 00:12:57.220
Here is your coffee.

00:13:04.040 --> 00:13:05.650
It's that same flavor, just as I thought.

00:13:06.540 --> 00:13:07.540
I've changed the way I make it.

00:13:07.740 --> 00:13:09.540
What!? I didn't give you any orders like that!

00:13:09.700 --> 00:13:11.200
I thought master would be pleased.

00:13:14.760 --> 00:13:16.630
Why'd you do that on your own?

00:13:17.350 --> 00:13:18.850
Even you're trying to imitate humans?

00:13:19.070 --> 00:13:20.700
I am an android.

00:13:20.840 --> 00:13:23.390
Master, I am not a human.

00:13:28.550 --> 00:13:31.280
What do you think of me?

00:13:33.150 --> 00:13:34.950
We look alike, but inside we're different.

00:13:35.170 --> 00:13:35.970
It's the other way around?

00:13:36.200 --> 00:13:39.300
We look the same, but inside we're different.

00:13:39.560 --> 00:13:41.650
I want to understand them better.

00:13:41.800 --> 00:13:44.020
After all, we're family.

00:13:50.510 --> 00:13:52.810
Hey, you're acting kind of android-holic.
